      "title": "cell_broadcast: Decode the CBS language indication",
      "message": "cell_broadcast: Decode the CBS language indication\n\n3GPP TS 23.038 clause 5 defines coding group 0001 as \"message\npreceded by language indication\", in two variants. With bits 0000\nthe message starts with the ISO 639 language code as two GSM 7 bit\ndefault alphabet characters followed by a CR. With bits 0001 it\nstarts with the same code as two packed septets padded to the octet\nboundary, ahead of UCS2 text.\n\nNeither was handled. SMS_ENCODING_UCS2_LANG shared the UCS2 case, so\nthe two language octets were decoded as if they were part of the\nUCS2 text and garbled the first character of the message.\nSMS_ENCODING_7BIT_LANG shared the GSM 7 bit case, which left the\nlanguage code and its CR inline in the message text.\n\nAdd a gsm_cbs.language field and decode the text only past the\nlanguage indication in both cases. Coding group 0000 carries its\nlanguage in the data coding scheme rather than in the message, so it\nkeeps all of its characters.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5)\n",
